  "response_text": "The stack allocation method used in the lab is based on the stack growing downwards. In the code we obtained the value for MSP-init_val which is a pointer to the start of the stack in memory.  Then, to obtain the value for PSP, MSP-init_val was casted to an int, then 0x400 was subtracted for it, which gave the value of PSP. It was required to know the initial value for MSP, because each new place in the stack is based on the starting location (which is held in MSP), and without knowing MSP, it would be impossible to traverse and add new locations in the stack.\\n",
